                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "You are presented with purple, light blue, green, gold and grey blood collection tubes. The examiner asks you to identify each tube, name its additive and match it to a laboratory investigation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Tasks"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify the additive in the purple-top tube and give two uses."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain why the light blue tube must be filled to the correct mark."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Identify a common tube for electrolyte testing."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Explain why EDTA contamination may increase measured potassium."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "State the usual order of draw for these tubes."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Give three reasons a laboratory may reject a specimen."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
